From: Dominik Krivohlavek <github@xkrivo.net>
Date: Wed, 4 Nov 2026 19:17:50 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 14/28] fix(midea): apply mop dock wash quirks to the custom
 pair too

The firmware uses the custom backwash area and wash mode instead of the
general ones whenever the mode byte of the mop dock settings is not 0.
The wash frequency and intensity quirks only changed the general pair,
so they had no effect after the vendor app selected a custom mode.

Write the new value into both pairs and leave the mode byte unchanged.
The getters still read the general pair.

Based on static analysis; untested. The code path is confirmed, that
mode != 0 means custom is likely.

diff --git a/backend/lib/robots/midea/MideaQuirkFactory.js b/backend/lib/robots/midea/MideaQuirkFactory.js
index 229c098e..103dd233 100644
--- a/backend/lib/robots/midea/MideaQuirkFactory.js
+++ b/backend/lib/robots/midea/MideaQuirkFactory.js
@@ -550,7 +550,7 @@ class MideaQuirkFactory {
                                     val,
                                     parsedResponse.general_cleaning_mode,
 
-                                    parsedResponse.custom_backwash_area,
+                                    val,
                                     parsedResponse.custom_cleaning_mode,
                                 ])
                             )
@@ -626,7 +626,7 @@ class MideaQuirkFactory {
                                     val,
 
                                     parsedResponse.custom_backwash_area,
-                                    parsedResponse.custom_cleaning_mode,
+                                    val,
                                 ])
                             )
                         }).toHexString());
